NASA Technical Standards

data/tables/design_factors_nasa.json and the flight-grade doctrine quote requirement
text, factors of safety and fastener rules from the following United States Government
works, each marked "APPROVED FOR PUBLIC RELEASE - DISTRIBUTION IS UNLIMITED". As works
of the U.S. Government they are not subject to copyright protection in the United States
(17 U.S.C. 105). NASA is acknowledged as the source.

  NASA-STD-5001B w/Change 3, "Structural Design and Test Factors of Safety for
    Spaceflight Hardware", change 3 dated 2022-10-24.
    https://standards.nasa.gov/standard/NASA/NASA-STD-5001
  NASA-STD-5020B, "Requirements for Threaded Fastening Systems in Spaceflight
    Hardware", approved 2021-08-06, revalidated 2026-01-05.
    https://standards.nasa.gov/standard/NASA/NASA-STD-5020

PartForge is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or certified by NASA. Nothing produced by
this tool is qualified to, or certified against, any NASA Technical Standard: a citation
records where a design rule came from, never conformance to it. These are spaceflight
criteria, and an amateur high-power rocket is not spaceflight hardware.

The NASA Insignia, the NASA Logotype, the NASA Seal and NASA program identifiers are NOT
in the public domain and are protected by law (14 CFR Part 1221). They are not used in
this project.

Where these standards normatively reference ASME, SAE, ASTM or ISO, a value that
originates with one of those bodies is cited to that body, not to NASA.

